#. §6: `==>`
#. §7: `refine ⟨32, ?_⟩`
#. §8: `py_check`
#. §9: `py_prove`
#: Game/Doc.lean:29
msgid "§0 fills in the goal with the expression §1, leaving every §2\n"
"inside §3 as a new goal.\n"
"\n"
"In this game its job is *supplying witnesses*. On an §4-goal,\n"
"§5 commits the value and leaves the claim about it open —\n"
"the find-the-input levels run on exactly this move. And every §6 goal is\n"
"secretly an existential too (“*some* amount of fuel makes this Python call\n"
"finish”), so the same move later donates the interpreter's fuel by hand:\n"
"§7 — exactly what §8 and §9 do for you\n"
"internally. Extra fuel is always harmless — a finished run keeps its\n"
"result."
msgstr ""

