#: Game/Doc.lean:143
msgid "§0 decides linear integer arithmetic goals: anything built from\n"
"§1/§2 variables with §3, §4, §5-by-constants, §6, §7, §8.\n"
"\n"
"Caveats learned in this game: §9 looks at the *head type* of each\n"
"comparison — a fact stated over the §10 brand is invisible to it (use\n"
"§11, which unfolds reducible definitions). It atomizes anything else it\n"
"doesn't understand — §12 is an opaque symbol to it, and §13\n"
"with both sides variables is out of its (linear) language. Inside its\n"
"language, though, it is a decision procedure: it *will* finish, e.g. by\n"
"refuting §14. **Trap to know**: on a branded goal, §15 may print a\n"
"plausible-looking counterexample that seems to contradict a hypothesis\n"
"sitting right in your context — it is not lying, it just *cannot see* the\n"
"branded hypothesis. If the counterexample looks impossible, reach for\n"
"§16."
msgstr ""

