#: Game/Levels/LoopWorld.lean:14
msgid "§0 loops. The programs are one honest step from real: countdowns,\n"
"Euclid's algorithm, trial division — and no finite case split covers any of\n"
"them, because the number of iterations depends on the input.\n"
"\n"
"What covers them is the oldest idea in program verification: the **loop\n"
"invariant** (a fact every iteration preserves) and the **decreasing\n"
"measure** (a number every iteration shrinks). These two are the content no\n"
"tactic can invent. Everything else — walking the code, splicing the symbolic\n"
"runs, forking the branches — is §1's job, and what it leaves you is\n"
"pure mathematics, tagged by role: §2, §3, §4, §5.\n"
"\n"
"You'll read one loop proof, then invent your own invariants — for a double\n"
"sum, for a square, for a countdown that shadows its own argument, for a\n"
"walk with a branch in its body, for Euclid — cash a corollary out of the\n"
"gcd theorem you bled for, and face the boss: a nested loop with a §6,\n"
"where you'll state what's true at the moment of escape."
msgstr ""

